WEBVTT

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:10.280
[Uhtred] <i>My name is Uhtred,</i>

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:10.280
<i>son of Uhtred.</i>

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:13.200
<i>I was born</i>

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:13.200
<i>an Aelderman of Northumbria,</i>

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.800
<i>the rightful heir</i>

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.800
<i>to Bebbanburg.</i>

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.760
<i>But fate decreed</i>

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.760
<i>I would be raised as a Dane.</i>

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.040
<i>That was my life.</i>

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.920
<i>Until my family was murdered.</i>

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:32.000
[yelling]

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.360
<i>Word was spread</i>

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.360
<i>that I was to blame.</i>

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.320
A Saxon slave, he killed his

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.320
master, at a wedding party.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.600
[Uhtred]<i> And so Brida</i>

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.600
<i>and I fled to Wessex.</i>

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:44.840
[crowd booing]

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:48.320
<i>To Alfred, a man</i>

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:48.320
<i>who would become king.</i>

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.040
<i>Though not all agreed.</i>

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.720
I am my father's heir!

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.880
[Uhtred]

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.880
<i>I swore an oath to this King</i>

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:58.840
<i>An oath that lost me Brida,</i>

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:58.840
<i>and prevented me</i>

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:01.400
<i>from joining</i>

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:01.400
<i>my brother, Ragnar.</i>

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:06.120
<i>But destiny is all.</i>

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.680
You don't deserve to marry.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.280
That woman is a lady,

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.280
and you are a heathen.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:03.840
You could bathe all day long

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.200
and you'd still

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.200
stink of pig shit.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.960
Have you been watching me,

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.960
Odda the Boy?

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.240
Should I be marrying you?

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:12.640
Ten pieces of silver

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:12.640
for you to walk away.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.040
Does your father

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.040
know you're here?

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.360
Eleven pieces.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:24.960
How about my sword's weight,

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:24.960
in silver?

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.120
Nonsense.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:33.160
Then I'll marry the girl,

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:33.160
and tonight, I'll plough her.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.120
Why must you

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.120
talk of her like that?

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:39.320
Perhaps you'd like her

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:39.320
for yourself Odda.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.080
You want her beneath you.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.080
Am I right?

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:45.880
You are impossible to reason

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:45.880
with, everything is a game.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.240
I hope for Mildrith's sake,

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:50.120
your time

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:50.120
on this earth is short.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:54.440
You are not an Aelderman...

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:54.440
and never shall be.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.320
[man commands horses]

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:18.800
[Uhtred] I wasn't allowed to

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:18.800
meet her. I haven't seen her.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.360
It is the way.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:24.720
I was unaware of her existence

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:24.720
until yesterday.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.200
She will be plain and pious.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.200
Oh, she'll be pious, alright.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:29.560
If she was a leg-spreader,

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.360
Alfred would have

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.360
been on her by now.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.200
Have you seen her?

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.400
A distance away.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:38.080
Plain is a fair description.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.120
-How much was the bride price?

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.120
-Thirty three pieces.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.040
Which I have paid,

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.040
to her Godfather Odda,

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:46.680
and which I'll make sure

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:46.680
she receives.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:53.600
I've made promises...

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:53.600
Revenge and such.

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:56.400
Why are you here? Do you know?

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:00.160
She brings land.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:00.160
I'll become a Lord under Alfred.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:03.400
I'll be able to make wealth;

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:03.400
gather men.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:06.800
-Take back what's mine.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:06.800
-All reasons enough.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.720
Plain or not,

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.720
she serves her purpose.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:12.040
The promises you have made

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:12.040
will stand.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:16.440
Blood feuds last a lifetime.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:16.440
What you do arseling,

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:19.280
is you keep living each day

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:19.280
until the last.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:26.600
The priest has arrived, finally,

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:26.600
let's get this done.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:30.160
You do not need

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:30.160
to get this done.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.640
I will make a plea to Alfred.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:41.480
She's here, praise God.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:45.280
You should stand and look respectful,

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:45.280
if not entirely clean.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:47.680
-How does she look?

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:47.680
-Terrified, I'll bet.

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:59.840
If you could be brief

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:59.840
with the ceremony Father Beocca,

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:03.560
I would be grateful.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:03.560
I have business with the king.

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:06.400
The bride

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:06.400
has been given her price?

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.920
She will.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.280
You are witness.

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:16.160
[woman]

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:16.160
Thank you, Lord.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:20.760
If the betrothed couple

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:20.760
would join me at the alter.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:26.160
-And join hands.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:26.160
-Be brief.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:49.920
May God in his Heaven,

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:49.920
look down with mercy

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.440
upon his devoted servants,

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.440
Uhtred and Mildrith;

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:57.080
may He bless their union with

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:57.080
love and children and wealth,

00:05:57.160 --> 00:06:01.360
and may they in turn,

00:05:57.160 --> 00:06:01.360
be sure to give thanks and praise

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:04.920
and live each day

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:04.920
according to His holy word.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.160
-Amen.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.160
-Amen.

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:09.200
Amen.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:12.560
You are now joined as man

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:12.560
and wife in the eyes of God.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:19.120
[sniffling]

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:21.040
Tears of joy.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:40.560
Allow me to help you with that.

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:44.280
Thank you, Lord.

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:51.440
I am a lucky man,

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:51.440
to have such a beautiful wife.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.520
There must have been

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.520
many suitors, I'm sure.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.560
You are kind to believe so.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:06:59.720
Am I right?

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:03.040
None suitable, Lord.

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:05.440
My name is Uhtred,

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:05.440
call me Uhtred.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:09.160
Arseling.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:09.160
Time we were on our way.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:13.240
Or from time-to-time you may

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:13.240
wish to call me arseling.

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:24.200
Lord...

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:28.160
Danes.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.280
[Mildrith]

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.280
Why are we stopping?

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:33.840
Who are they?

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:36.600
Foragers most likely.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:38.560
But Danes all the same.

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:40.200
Will they attack?

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:42.360
We walk on.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:48.760
[Mildrith]

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:48.760
They're following us.

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:51.040
[Uhtred]

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:51.040
We walk on. They won't attack.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:55.200
Then why have you

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:55.200
drawn your sword?

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:58.000
To show them at least

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:58.000
one of them will die.

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:01.120
One or two.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:04.120
For foragers

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:04.120
they're deep into Wessex.

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:06.160
They're Guthrum's men.

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:08.800
They're a long way

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:08.800
from Lundene.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:15.800
[door opens]

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:19.080
Lord, the marriage

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:19.080
has taken place.

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:21.360
They are now on the road

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:21.360
to the farmstead.

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:24.200
Good news. Thank you, Odda.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:28.400
We shall now see how he

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:28.400
responds to the challenge.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:31.840
Now it is done, Lord,

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:31.840
I do fear for Mildrith.

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:35.040
She will have to

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:35.040
give him the facts.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:39.240
Oh, he will bark at her,

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:39.240
Odda, I am sure.

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:42.520
But his real anger will be

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:42.520
reserved for you and I.

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:45.280
He will not like being beholden

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:45.280
to God and to king,

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:47.720
but if he is to become

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:47.720
a true Aelderman...

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:49.200
[inhalees deeply]

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:52.040
...he must accept his burden,

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:52.040
that is the test.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:54.240
Yes, Lord.

00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:00.480
Mildrith is his

00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:00.480
beautiful consolation.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.040
[chuckles]

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.240
Was he struck by her?

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:10.720
He was, Lord.

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:21.920
Why have you

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:21.920
not already married?

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:24.440
You're old enough to have had

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:26.360
two or three children by now.

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:31.120
Lord Arseling, there is a time for

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:31.120
such questions and it has past.

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:34.240
Why has Alfred gifted me

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:34.240
such a beautiful bride?

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:39.680
Has a debt, I'm guessing.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:42.880
It's not my place

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:42.880
to tell you.

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:47.200
How much?

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:51.600
My father wanted to

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:51.600
find favor with God,

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:54.960
so he devoted a tenth

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:54.960
of his land to the church.

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:58.680
They do not own it, but they

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:58.680
are entitled to its yield;

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:01.880
indeed they demand its yield,

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:05.000
even when crops fail

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:05.000
and Danes raid.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:06.200
God is good.

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:09.480
So the Bishop

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:09.480
took my father to law.

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:10.960
How much is the debt?

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:14.160
The church is the law,

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:14.160
and the law decreed

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:16.120
that my father

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:16.120
owed to them a huge sum,

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:18.200
quite beyond

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:18.200
his ability to pay.

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:20.040
How much?

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:24.040
He died soon after.

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:32.680
It is a substantial amount,

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:32.680
Lord, it increases yearly.

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:35.560
Alfred could remove the debt,

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:35.560
but he has chosen not to.

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:38.760
The amount owed

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:38.760
is 2,000 shillings, Lord.

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:40.640
[chuckles]

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:42.760
Damn him.

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:46.400
Damn everything he stands for.

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:47.560
Damn his church.

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:49.200
-Damn his God--

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:49.200
-Lord, I must say

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:51.960
-I do not like your blasphemy.

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:51.960
-My name is Uhtred!

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:03.800
Though by all means call me arseling

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:03.800
for not seeing this sooner.

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:12.440
[indistinct chatter in distance]

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:21.280
[Mildrith]

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:21.280
Your new home, Lord.

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:24.240
The land is good but the

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:24.240
buildings are in need of repair.

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:25.920
Look, the families

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:25.920
who live on the land

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:27.520
have come to wish us well.

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:29.880
Send them back to their homes.

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:32.560
They have come to wish us well.

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:34.920
I have known them my whole life.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.400
Lord... Lady.

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:40.680
Oswald manages the farmstead,

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:40.680
he lives nearby.

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:42.440
Welcome home.

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:44.800
And may we offer our

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:44.800
good wishes on your marriage.

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:47.120
Thank you, Oswald, thank you.

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:51.160
And how kind of you all to gather

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:51.160
and to greet me and my Lord, Uhtred.

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:54.720
We have prepared a table,

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:54.720
Lord, for your pleasure.

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:58.280
You have my thanks,

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:58.280
but we're tired.

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:01.000
Of course, Lord.

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:03.400
[chuckles]

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:06.880
Thank you, Oswald, you are kind.

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:09.880
I have a wedding gift,

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:09.880
for each family.

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:12.480
-Tis silver...

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:12.480
-Thank you, Lady Mildrith.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:15.240
...for your kindness

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:15.240
and your loyalty.

00:12:15.320 --> 00:12:16.720
Thank you, so much.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:18.960
For taking care of the land

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:18.960
in my prolonged absence.

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:26.280
Now there's a welcome sight.

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:37.760
I was expecting there to be

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:37.760
a hall and I find a this.

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:40.880
Pay off your debts

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:40.880
and you can build a hall.

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:44.720
Didn't I tell you

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:44.720
the bastard thinks? Alfred.

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:47.400
If he believes

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:47.400
he can make me beg,

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:49.280
he can think again.

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:53.480
He doesn't want you to beg,

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:53.480
he wants you to obey.

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:55.880
Never.

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:58.720
If you have need for me Lord,

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:58.720
I will be resting.

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:00.680
It seems I am tired.

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:03.240
I am 2,000 shillings in

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:03.240
debt to the church

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:05.400
and you hand out

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:05.400
silver to your tenants.

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:08.040
It is my silver.

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:10.200
You can have what's in my purse.

00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:12.120
I don't want

00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:12.120
what is in your purse.

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:14.040
Then why scold me?

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:21.480
The stoat;

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:21.480
your farmstead master.

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:24.200
-His name is Oswald.

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:24.200
-He'll need to be watched.

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:25.800
He was trusted by my father.

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:27.400
He lives too well

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:27.400
by the look of him.

00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:28.920
I'll make my way to the barn.

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:32.040
You're a guest;

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:32.040
you can sleep in the house.

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:34.920
I prefer the barn. Thank you.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:36.440
It is your wedding night.

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:40.720
Goodnight lady.

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:40.720
Arseling.

00:13:49.440 --> 00:13:51.360
May I leave now?

00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:55.800
How many pieces of silver did

00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:55.800
you receive, as your price?

00:13:55.880 --> 00:13:57.480
Eighteen.

00:13:57.560 --> 00:14:00.320
Is that correct?

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:02.880
The price was 33.

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:05.200
I'm sure

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:05.200
it was a honest mistake.

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:09.320
You were robbed.

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:09.320
As I was robbed!

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:14.440
That price is your security

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:14.440
and you will have it, all of it.

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:18.000
May I rest?

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:22.800
Yes.

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:27.320
I am sorry the day has been

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:27.320
a disappointment for you Lord...

00:14:28.280 --> 00:14:30.080
...for us both.

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:53.200
[digging sound]

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:03.840
[water sloshes]

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:29.440
You have a good heart,

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:29.440
gifting your silver.

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:34.000
Odda owes you 15 pieces more,

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:36.680
I'll see that he pays.

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:39.440
And the debt's not

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:39.440
something I blame you for.

00:15:40.360 --> 00:15:42.240
It's Alfred's deceit.

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:44.680
I should have been wiser.

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:49.840
Though I was blinded by you.

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:01.880
You should eat.

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:05.400
I should eat,

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:05.400
but I don't want to eat alone.

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:11.760
God has made me your wife.

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:11.760
There must be a reason.

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:14.320
God is good.

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:14.960
What is it you are looking at?

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:25.800
There's a scar across the land;

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:30.280
there, the never ending line

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:30.280
of Danes on the march.

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:33.640
Ragnar.

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:41.760
By the time word reaches

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:41.760
Alfred it will be too late.

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:44.800
They would need wings.

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:47.400
Go.

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:54.920
Oswald, what town

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:54.920
lays in that direction?

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:56.400
If they keep going to the west,

00:17:56.480 --> 00:17:59.200
in a day or so they'll come

00:17:56.480 --> 00:17:59.200
to the fortress, at Werham.

00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:02.760
Take your family

00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:02.760
and the others to the hills

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:04.840
'til we're sure they've passed.

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:04.840
Do it now.

00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:06.200
And the Lady Mildrith?

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:10.040
She travels with me...

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:10.040
to Winchester.

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:12.320
[Oswald] Yes, Lord.

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:18.920
[Leofric]

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:18.920
How many do you see?

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:21.240
The question is

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:21.240
how many will follow?

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:28.640
[Uhtred]

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:28.640
Wessex is being invaded

00:18:28.720 --> 00:18:31.600
and we're told to wait

00:18:28.720 --> 00:18:31.600
while he prays.

00:18:31.680 --> 00:18:33.600
God is his strength, Uhtred.

00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:36.400
He needs to be on horseback,

00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:36.400
not on his knees.

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:42.240
-I hate this place.

00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:42.240
-It grows worse.

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:48.120
Mildrith.

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:48.120
I was not told you were here.

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:50.280
-How pleasing to see you.

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:50.280
-Lord.

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:51.680
And so much of you.

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:53.360
[Uhtred]

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:53.360
Is he ready?

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:56.520
The king is ready,

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:56.520
as is his council.

00:18:57.680 --> 00:18:59.320
With me.

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:09.480
You watched 300 men or more

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:09.480
march clean across

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:11.360
Wessex and you did nothing?

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:14.400
I'm here.

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:18.440
A messenger could have been

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:18.440
sent in your place, a boy.

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:20.320
Why did you not

00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:20.320
confront these Danes?

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:22.680
You have men. That is your purpose,

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:22.680
to create warriors.

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:24.960
I have been given

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:24.960
barely 20 men and their wives,

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:26.200
most of whom work the fields.

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:27.920
It would have been

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:27.920
a slaughter, Lord.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:30.040
[Odda the Elder] But you chose

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:30.040
not to fight; we'll never know.

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:32.920
A warrior can only die once!

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:32.920
Why die in vain?

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.920
The Danes have traveled from

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.920
either Lundene or East Anglia.

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:37.160
Were they not being watched?

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:39.960
We have been watching the ships,

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:39.960
which remain on the Tames.

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:42.040
A mistake.

00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:44.000
If Werham is captured,

00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:44.000
the ships will follow,

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:46.440
300 men will become 3,000.

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:48.640
My advice is that we march,

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:48.640
without delay.

00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:50.560
I don't recall

00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:50.560
the King seeking your advice.

00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:53.200
Leofric, my trusted man,

00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:53.200
how many Danes did you witness?

00:19:53.280 --> 00:19:55.960
More than two hundred, by far.

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:58.280
Warriors to a man.

00:19:58.360 --> 00:20:00.560
Werham will struggle

00:19:58.360 --> 00:20:00.560
to hold them back.

00:20:00.640 --> 00:20:03.320
The peace is over.

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:06.000
We have no choice

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:06.000
but to march on Werham

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:09.040
and pray God we arrive

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:09.040
before the fortress falls.

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:11.160
You believe

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:11.160
it is an invasion, Lord?

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:14.640
It could well be the beginning

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:14.640
of the great Dane army, yes.

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:18.120
Council is over. Aeldermen of

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:18.120
Wessex, prepare your men.

00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:19.920
Father Beocca!

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:23.040
-I shall pray before we leave.

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:23.040
-Yes, my Lord.

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:28.080
Father. I wish to speak

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:28.080
to the king, privately?

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:29.520
I will ask.

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:32.400
But I note that you are

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:32.400
still to learn respect.

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:39.800
Aelderman Odda,

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:39.800
if I may speak out.

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:43.560
You owe my wife

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:43.560
half of her bride price.

00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:47.360
I paid 33 pieces of silver,

00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:47.360
she received only 18.

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:49.640
An honest mistake,

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:49.640
she assures me.

00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:55.040
Is this true?

00:20:59.240 --> 00:21:01.120
Pay him.

00:21:04.720 --> 00:21:07.680
Ready the men

00:21:04.720 --> 00:21:07.680
to march on Werham.

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:13.000
You should know that Mildrith

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:13.000
is a joy to plough.

00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:15.120
You are heathen.

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:20.680
-And you're a virgin.

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:20.680
-No, I'm not.

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:25.200
[door opens]

00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:27.240
Yes, he is!

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:33.800
[indistinct chatter]

00:21:51.040 --> 00:21:52.480
What is it?

00:21:52.560 --> 00:21:53.560
Hmm?

00:21:53.640 --> 00:21:55.960
Promise me

00:21:53.640 --> 00:21:55.960
you will come back safely.

00:21:57.240 --> 00:22:01.080
-Two arms, both ears.

00:21:57.240 --> 00:22:01.080
-Promise me.

00:22:02.200 --> 00:22:07.640
I'll do my best...

00:22:02.200 --> 00:22:07.640
but only if you do the same.

00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:10.000
If they come, don't shelter

00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:10.000
in a church or nunnery;

00:22:10.080 --> 00:22:14.160
go to the hills,

00:22:10.080 --> 00:22:14.160
the woods and I'll come...

00:22:16.920 --> 00:22:19.040
...for both of you.

00:22:20.080 --> 00:22:21.400
[Leofric] Arseling!

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:23.960
Kiss her,

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:23.960
and let's be on our way.

00:23:38.760 --> 00:23:41.920
Mildrith, my dear,

00:23:38.760 --> 00:23:41.920
I have been looking for you.

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:43.440
My Lady Aelswith!

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:45.960
How good to see you and to

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:45.960
see you looking as you do.

00:23:46.040 --> 00:23:49.120
-It refuses to keep still.

00:23:46.040 --> 00:23:49.120
-Mine is the same.

00:23:49.200 --> 00:23:50.880
Oh, how we suffer.

00:23:50.960 --> 00:23:54.720
I pray we both survive;

00:23:50.960 --> 00:23:54.720
I pray we four survive.

00:23:54.800 --> 00:23:56.520
God will decide.

00:23:58.000 --> 00:23:59.360
I have missed you, Mildrith,

00:23:59.440 --> 00:24:03.160
and prayed for you each day,

00:23:59.440 --> 00:24:03.160
you poor thing.

00:24:03.240 --> 00:24:04.640
Why poor?

00:24:04.720 --> 00:24:08.240
Living with the man they foisted

00:24:04.720 --> 00:24:08.240
onto you, the Pagan.

00:24:08.320 --> 00:24:11.680
Having to take his seed

00:24:08.320 --> 00:24:11.680
and the like.

00:24:11.760 --> 00:24:17.160
Uhtred is decent.

00:24:11.760 --> 00:24:17.160
He treats me well... He does.

00:24:17.240 --> 00:24:20.000
God will bless your loyalty,

00:24:20.080 --> 00:24:25.000
but with luck he will

00:24:20.080 --> 00:24:25.000
fall in battle, and soon.

00:24:27.960 --> 00:24:29.960
Please, tell me

00:24:27.960 --> 00:24:29.960
that you're hungry.

00:24:30.040 --> 00:24:31.640
I am... a little.

00:24:31.720 --> 00:24:35.480
Meet me in kitchens. I have

00:24:31.720 --> 00:24:35.480
arranged a meal for the pregnant.

00:24:35.560 --> 00:24:39.640
-But do not rush prayers.

00:24:35.560 --> 00:24:39.640
-No, no, of course not.

00:24:46.600 --> 00:24:50.240
[door opens, closes]

00:24:50.320 --> 00:24:53.280
Oh, Lord, he is not

00:24:50.320 --> 00:24:53.280
your most humble

00:24:53.360 --> 00:24:59.280
or devout servant,

00:24:53.360 --> 00:24:59.280
but I pray, keep him safe.

00:24:59.360 --> 00:25:04.680
Let him do your work,

00:24:59.360 --> 00:25:04.680
let him see his child.

00:25:08.840 --> 00:25:10.560
I was pleased to see

00:25:08.840 --> 00:25:10.560
your lady today;

00:25:10.640 --> 00:25:14.400
your wife...

00:25:10.640 --> 00:25:14.400
and carrying a child.

00:25:14.480 --> 00:25:18.040
-Yes.

00:25:14.480 --> 00:25:18.040
-It's God's blessing.

00:25:18.840 --> 00:25:20.640
It seems like only yesterday,

00:25:20.720 --> 00:25:24.200
I was baptizing you as Osbert,

00:25:20.720 --> 00:25:24.200
and then again as Uhtred.

00:25:26.520 --> 00:25:28.960
What is it you wish

00:25:26.520 --> 00:25:28.960
to speak about with the king?

00:25:29.040 --> 00:25:31.480
That's between

00:25:29.040 --> 00:25:31.480
myself and the king.

00:25:31.560 --> 00:25:33.640
He is watching you Uhtred.

00:25:33.720 --> 00:25:36.480
-God?

00:25:33.720 --> 00:25:36.480
-Alfred...

00:25:36.560 --> 00:25:37.480
He's watching how you behave.

00:25:37.560 --> 00:25:38.720
He's judging you as a Lord.

00:25:39.000 --> 00:25:40.920
He has no right to judge.

00:25:41.000 --> 00:25:42.800
He's a king.

00:25:44.520 --> 00:25:47.680
He lied to me

00:25:44.520 --> 00:25:47.680
regarding the marriage.

00:25:47.760 --> 00:25:49.600
Are you referring to the debt?

00:25:49.680 --> 00:25:52.320
-You know of it?

00:25:49.680 --> 00:25:52.320
-It's not a secret.

00:25:52.400 --> 00:25:55.080
And I urge you to show him

00:25:52.400 --> 00:25:55.080
you accept it;

00:25:55.160 --> 00:25:58.080
especially as it is

00:25:55.160 --> 00:25:58.080
owed to the church.

00:25:59.320 --> 00:26:03.120
You must remain calm, Uhtred;

00:25:59.320 --> 00:26:03.120
respectful.

00:26:12.520 --> 00:26:13.880
My Lord.

00:26:13.960 --> 00:26:16.560
-I requested a private--

00:26:13.960 --> 00:26:16.560
-Have you eaten?

00:26:18.800 --> 00:26:20.440
No.

00:26:21.800 --> 00:26:26.960
There are times

00:26:21.800 --> 00:26:26.960
when I crave meat...

00:26:28.080 --> 00:26:30.600
...and other things.

00:26:30.680 --> 00:26:33.200
But I know the gratification

00:26:30.680 --> 00:26:33.200
would be fleeting;

00:26:33.280 --> 00:26:37.400
the suffering prolonged,

00:26:33.280 --> 00:26:37.400
and so I suffer gruel.

00:26:37.480 --> 00:26:42.360
Though my wife will not allow it to

00:26:37.480 --> 00:26:42.360
be called anything other than broth.

00:26:42.440 --> 00:26:45.480
You will be happy to learn

00:26:42.440 --> 00:26:45.480
that my spies have news.

00:26:45.560 --> 00:26:48.320
-From Werham?

00:26:45.560 --> 00:26:48.320
-From Ireland.

00:26:48.400 --> 00:26:51.200
Ivar, the brother of Ubba,

00:26:48.400 --> 00:26:51.200
has been killed there.

00:26:51.280 --> 00:26:53.040
Which would be irrelevant

00:26:51.280 --> 00:26:53.040
but for the fact

00:26:53.120 --> 00:26:55.520
that Ubba wishes

00:26:53.120 --> 00:26:55.520
to avenge him, personally.

00:26:55.600 --> 00:26:57.240
This is true?

00:26:58.680 --> 00:27:03.960
An Irishman across the sea kills

00:26:58.680 --> 00:27:03.960
a Dane and the world changes.

00:27:04.040 --> 00:27:06.480
The hand of God.

00:27:08.920 --> 00:27:12.080
Is this something

00:27:08.920 --> 00:27:12.080
Ubba would do, abandon Guthrum?

00:27:12.160 --> 00:27:16.400
To avenge his brother, yes, if

00:27:12.160 --> 00:27:16.400
guided by his sorcerer's story.

00:27:17.280 --> 00:27:19.560
He has a sorcerer?

00:27:20.920 --> 00:27:23.880
And...

00:27:20.920 --> 00:27:23.880
what does this sorcerer do,

00:27:23.960 --> 00:27:25.720
cast spells, perform magic?

00:27:25.800 --> 00:27:31.040
He advises, Lord. He looks for omens,

00:27:25.800 --> 00:27:31.040
signs, good and bad.

00:27:31.120 --> 00:27:33.520
Oh, what nonsense.

00:27:34.480 --> 00:27:37.040
What are miracles, Lord,

00:27:34.480 --> 00:27:37.040
if not magic?

00:27:37.120 --> 00:27:39.640
Miracles are performed by God,

00:27:37.120 --> 00:27:39.640
not man.

00:27:39.720 --> 00:27:40.840
The Danes would say the same,

00:27:40.920 --> 00:27:42.400
that omens are gifts

00:27:40.920 --> 00:27:42.400
from the gods.

00:27:42.480 --> 00:27:43.920
And they are mistaken.

00:27:44.000 --> 00:27:46.240
Who gave the sign

00:27:44.000 --> 00:27:46.240
for Ubba to go to Ireland,

00:27:46.320 --> 00:27:48.080
was that the hand

00:27:46.320 --> 00:27:48.080
of your God? Or theirs?

00:27:48.160 --> 00:27:49.800
There is only one God.

00:27:49.880 --> 00:27:52.520
Then he must have

00:27:49.880 --> 00:27:52.520
spoken to the Danes.

00:27:54.560 --> 00:27:55.920
With Ubba now in Ireland;

00:27:56.000 --> 00:27:59.400
Guthrum must now decide

00:27:56.000 --> 00:27:59.400
whether he will fight alone.

00:27:59.480 --> 00:28:03.800
He won't fight alone,

00:27:59.480 --> 00:28:03.800
not that he couldn't win.

00:28:03.880 --> 00:28:06.440
He will fear losing

00:28:03.880 --> 00:28:06.440
too many of his own men?

00:28:06.520 --> 00:28:08.800
Yes, Lord.

00:28:08.880 --> 00:28:14.520
I am learning that the heathen

00:28:08.880 --> 00:28:14.520
cares only for personal gain.

00:28:14.600 --> 00:28:18.040
A Dane could never

00:28:14.600 --> 00:28:18.040
suffer my gruel.

00:28:18.120 --> 00:28:20.720
Broth, Lord.

00:28:22.920 --> 00:28:27.000
You are happy,

00:28:22.920 --> 00:28:27.000
Aelderman Uhtred, with Mildrith?

00:28:28.000 --> 00:28:30.720
Yes, Lord. She's a good wife.

00:28:32.400 --> 00:28:36.280
Though, I never would of married her

00:28:32.400 --> 00:28:36.280
had I known I' owe 2,000 shillings.

00:28:36.360 --> 00:28:37.280
Which increases yearly.

00:28:37.360 --> 00:28:39.480
I am told that on your word

00:28:37.360 --> 00:28:39.480
the debt can be lifted.

00:28:39.560 --> 00:28:41.880
Why should I deny

00:28:39.560 --> 00:28:41.880
the church 2,000 shillings?

00:28:41.960 --> 00:28:45.760
-I wasn't aware I'd owe it.

00:28:41.960 --> 00:28:45.760
-It is not a secret.

00:28:47.240 --> 00:28:50.520
Sacrifice and penance are what

00:28:47.240 --> 00:28:50.520
separate us from the heathen.

00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:54.840
I have my broth,

00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:54.840
you have your debt.

00:28:57.000 --> 00:28:59.560
Wessex needs an army,

00:28:57.000 --> 00:28:59.560
would you agree?

00:28:59.640 --> 00:29:04.760
A permanent

00:28:59.640 --> 00:29:04.760
and formidable army?

00:29:06.440 --> 00:29:09.320
Yes, Lord.

00:29:09.400 --> 00:29:12.000
England,

00:29:09.400 --> 00:29:12.000
when it finally emerges,

00:29:12.080 --> 00:29:14.160
shall need a greater army.

00:29:14.240 --> 00:29:19.800
Garrisons of many thousands of men,

00:29:14.240 --> 00:29:19.800
all will need feeding, and payment.

00:29:19.880 --> 00:29:22.200
It is my intention

00:29:19.880 --> 00:29:22.200
that all land owners

00:29:22.280 --> 00:29:26.080
shall contribute to the feeding

00:29:22.280 --> 00:29:26.080
of this army and its commanders.

00:29:27.200 --> 00:29:30.000
And I will need

00:29:27.200 --> 00:29:30.000
commanders, Uhtred.

00:29:30.320 --> 00:29:34.840
Men like the great

00:29:30.320 --> 00:29:34.840
generals of Rome.

00:29:36.880 --> 00:29:39.760
Look upon the debt as a gift;

00:29:39.840 --> 00:29:44.120
a means of proving your devotion

00:29:39.840 --> 00:29:44.120
to Wessex and to England.

00:29:44.200 --> 00:29:46.600
If I'd been told the truth from the

00:29:44.200 --> 00:29:46.600
outset, Lord, I could've--

00:29:46.680 --> 00:29:48.840
You still wear

00:29:46.680 --> 00:29:48.840
the amulet, I see.

00:29:50.320 --> 00:29:51.800
To remind me of Earl Ragnar.

00:29:51.880 --> 00:29:53.640
And why do you not attend

00:29:51.880 --> 00:29:53.640
church with your wife?

00:29:53.720 --> 00:29:55.200
Why do you not pray to God?

00:29:55.280 --> 00:29:59.320
God created everything

00:29:55.280 --> 00:29:59.320
that surrounds me:

00:29:59.400 --> 00:30:01.080
the fields, rivers, the forest.

00:30:01.160 --> 00:30:02.760
The land is my church.

00:30:02.840 --> 00:30:08.680
And I pray each day,

00:30:02.840 --> 00:30:08.680
Lord, in silence.

00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:30.440
-He cannot be tamed.

00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:30.440
-But he can be trusted.

00:30:31.720 --> 00:30:35.680
I will not

00:30:31.720 --> 00:30:35.680
abandon him completely.

00:30:35.760 --> 00:30:38.840
He may have a use, I'm sure.

00:30:46.400 --> 00:30:49.840
[metal clanging]

00:30:49.920 --> 00:30:53.000
Hear me now!

00:30:49.920 --> 00:30:53.000
Werham has fallen!

00:30:53.080 --> 00:30:54.960
We march at once!

00:30:55.040 --> 00:30:58.520
Every man is to be ready

00:30:55.040 --> 00:30:58.520
to do as the king asks.

00:30:58.600 --> 00:31:01.640
The Danes

00:30:58.600 --> 00:31:01.640
have taken the fortress!

00:31:01.720 --> 00:31:04.120
Werham has fallen!

00:31:01.720 --> 00:31:04.120
We march at once!

00:31:04.200 --> 00:31:07.960
We could be slipping in blood and

00:31:04.200 --> 00:31:07.960
entrails before the day is out.

00:31:08.040 --> 00:31:09.760
With luck.

00:31:30.760 --> 00:31:33.160
[indistinct chatter]

00:31:40.840 --> 00:31:43.280
Leave him,

00:31:40.840 --> 00:31:43.280
there is enough for everyone.

00:31:50.640 --> 00:31:51.920
[door opens]

00:31:52.000 --> 00:31:53.800
[Young Ragnar]

00:31:52.000 --> 00:31:53.800
Guthrum? They're here.

00:31:55.000 --> 00:31:57.200
The Saxon army is gathering.

00:31:57.280 --> 00:31:59.080
-Is it Alfred?

00:31:57.280 --> 00:31:59.080
-Yes.

00:32:01.600 --> 00:32:04.000
Is the fortress

00:32:01.600 --> 00:32:04.000
repaired and secure?

00:32:04.080 --> 00:32:05.600
Yes.

00:32:05.680 --> 00:32:09.560
Good. He will not attack.

00:32:05.680 --> 00:32:09.560
He doesn't need to.

00:32:09.640 --> 00:32:11.600
He knows we will be

00:32:09.640 --> 00:32:11.600
hungry within days.

00:32:11.680 --> 00:32:13.320
We can raid.

00:32:13.400 --> 00:32:18.760
No, he will empty all the grain-stores,

00:32:13.400 --> 00:32:18.760
in the surrounding villages.

00:32:20.600 --> 00:32:23.480
I have found these church rooms

00:32:23.560 --> 00:32:27.200
to be strangely quiet and peaceful.

00:32:27.280 --> 00:32:29.960
Lord, I didn't march my men

00:32:30.040 --> 00:32:32.880
half way across England

00:32:30.040 --> 00:32:32.880
for them to starve.

00:32:33.800 --> 00:32:35.520
I shall be on the ramparts.

00:32:35.600 --> 00:32:39.680
We came for war Ragnar,

00:32:35.600 --> 00:32:39.680
but Ubba has reneged.

00:32:39.760 --> 00:32:41.680
To avenge his brother.

00:32:41.760 --> 00:32:43.680
You are here.

00:32:44.960 --> 00:32:48.520
Should you not be

00:32:44.960 --> 00:32:48.520
avenging your father?

00:32:49.280 --> 00:32:50.520
When the time is right.

00:32:50.600 --> 00:32:55.240
Yes! When the time is right.

00:32:56.840 --> 00:33:00.440
We have taken the first steps

00:32:56.840 --> 00:33:00.440
against Wessex!

00:33:01.560 --> 00:33:07.640
But Ubba has left us weak,

00:33:01.560 --> 00:33:07.640
he put all of our of lives at risk.

00:33:07.720 --> 00:33:13.080
So until Ubba returns,

00:33:07.720 --> 00:33:13.080
we have to make peace.

00:33:20.800 --> 00:33:22.640
[grunts]

00:33:25.160 --> 00:33:27.400
So if you are there,

00:33:28.240 --> 00:33:32.960
God of Rome, strike me down.

00:33:35.560 --> 00:33:37.720
I thought not.

00:33:40.080 --> 00:33:42.320
We are here to show them

00:33:40.080 --> 00:33:42.320
how many we are.

00:33:42.400 --> 00:33:46.520
We are here to show them

00:33:42.400 --> 00:33:46.520
how many we are.

00:33:46.600 --> 00:33:50.680
That we are here with God,

00:33:46.600 --> 00:33:50.680
and that is our land.

00:33:50.760 --> 00:33:53.480
That we are here with God,

00:33:53.560 --> 00:33:55.480
and this is our land.

00:33:56.240 --> 00:34:00.960
This is our land, our Wessex.

00:34:01.040 --> 00:34:02.960
This is our England!

00:34:03.040 --> 00:34:04.560
[crowd murmurs]

00:34:04.640 --> 00:34:08.680
And we shall murder any heathen

00:34:04.640 --> 00:34:08.680
bastard that tries to take it!

00:34:08.760 --> 00:34:11.120
[all cheering]

00:34:29.720 --> 00:34:31.080
They wish to talk, Lord.

00:34:31.160 --> 00:34:34.840
I know what they want.

00:34:31.160 --> 00:34:34.840
They want time.

00:34:34.920 --> 00:34:37.720
Odda, with your guards,

00:34:34.920 --> 00:34:37.720
you shall go with me.

00:34:37.800 --> 00:34:38.920
Leofric, you as well.

00:34:39.000 --> 00:34:40.920
And Father Selbix.

00:34:41.000 --> 00:34:42.480
Yes, Lord.

00:34:42.560 --> 00:34:44.760
Leofric, what do you

00:34:42.560 --> 00:34:44.760
make of the fortress?

00:34:44.840 --> 00:34:47.600
It looks strong enough, Lord.

00:34:47.680 --> 00:34:51.360
No breech,

00:34:47.680 --> 00:34:51.360
no signs of lasting damage.

00:34:51.440 --> 00:34:53.680
And if we attacked?

00:34:54.640 --> 00:34:57.360
We would suffer.

00:34:57.440 --> 00:35:00.120
We'd be lucky

00:34:57.440 --> 00:35:00.120
to see the inside, Lord.

00:35:01.760 --> 00:35:03.840
Good morning, King Alfred.

00:35:03.920 --> 00:35:05.960
Guthrum of the Danes.

00:35:06.040 --> 00:35:09.200
I too am a king now,

00:35:06.040 --> 00:35:09.200
of East Anglia.

00:35:09.280 --> 00:35:11.720
You don't need to bow.

00:35:12.880 --> 00:35:17.680
I will begin.

00:35:12.880 --> 00:35:17.680
I propose a truce.

00:35:17.760 --> 00:35:19.600
For any truce to occur,

00:35:17.760 --> 00:35:19.600
Earl Guthrum,

00:35:19.680 --> 00:35:21.720
you must leave Wessex,

00:35:19.680 --> 00:35:21.720
once again.

00:35:21.800 --> 00:35:24.360
-And if I refuse?

00:35:21.800 --> 00:35:24.360
-We surround you.

00:35:24.440 --> 00:35:26.000
Yes, you surround

00:35:24.440 --> 00:35:26.000
a small fortress,

00:35:26.080 --> 00:35:28.000
but we Danes

00:35:26.080 --> 00:35:28.000
surround your entire Kingdom.

00:35:28.080 --> 00:35:32.720
That said, I have decided

00:35:28.080 --> 00:35:32.720
I shall leave by sea.

00:35:32.800 --> 00:35:35.080
Therefore,

00:35:32.800 --> 00:35:35.080
I will send for ships.

00:35:35.160 --> 00:35:37.760
-How many ships?

00:35:35.160 --> 00:35:37.760
-No more than 15.

00:35:37.840 --> 00:35:42.280
Very well, your ships have

00:35:37.840 --> 00:35:42.280
one month in which to arrive.

00:35:42.360 --> 00:35:43.360
Not enough time.

00:35:43.440 --> 00:35:45.560
Food and ale for one month only,

00:35:45.640 --> 00:35:48.360
or you will

00:35:45.640 --> 00:35:48.360
walk back to East Anglia.

00:35:48.440 --> 00:35:51.840
Then I will send for 200 ships and

00:35:48.440 --> 00:35:51.840
hope they arrive before we starve.

00:35:51.920 --> 00:35:54.840
-One month is not enough.

00:35:51.920 --> 00:35:54.840
-That is my limit.

00:35:54.920 --> 00:35:57.120
You cannot take back

00:35:54.920 --> 00:35:57.120
the fortress, you know this.

00:35:57.200 --> 00:36:00.240
Food and ale for one month,

00:35:57.200 --> 00:36:00.240
no more,

00:36:00.320 --> 00:36:05.040
by which time the sea storms

00:36:00.320 --> 00:36:05.040
will have arrived, God's storms.

00:36:05.120 --> 00:36:07.960
We will be gone within a month,

00:36:08.040 --> 00:36:11.240
beginning upon the

00:36:08.040 --> 00:36:11.240
delivery of food and ale.

00:36:21.520 --> 00:36:24.720
Uhtred, you will come to me

00:36:21.520 --> 00:36:24.720
following prayers.

00:36:24.800 --> 00:36:25.920
Yes, Lord.

00:36:26.000 --> 00:36:28.400
Father Selbix,

00:36:26.000 --> 00:36:28.400
you will pray with me.

00:36:28.480 --> 00:36:30.040
Yes, Lord.

00:36:34.280 --> 00:36:36.160
[Alfred]

00:36:34.280 --> 00:36:36.160
Please, sit.

00:36:40.000 --> 00:36:41.880
Thank you, Lord.

00:36:44.080 --> 00:36:46.640
I have a task for you, Father.

00:36:46.720 --> 00:36:50.120
You only have to speak it.

00:36:50.840 --> 00:36:52.640
As a guarantee of the peace,

00:36:52.720 --> 00:36:55.240
you will be given up

00:36:52.720 --> 00:36:55.240
as a hostage; one of ten.

00:36:55.320 --> 00:36:59.040
The Danes, too,

00:36:55.320 --> 00:36:59.040
will give ten in exchange.

00:37:01.400 --> 00:37:06.680
Lord, the Pagans

00:37:01.400 --> 00:37:06.680
do not value priests.

00:37:06.760 --> 00:37:09.280
You might just as well

00:37:06.760 --> 00:37:09.280
offer a hound.

00:37:09.360 --> 00:37:11.640
I hear Guthrum

00:37:09.360 --> 00:37:11.640
is curious about our faith.

00:37:11.720 --> 00:37:17.520
I would like you to become his

00:37:11.720 --> 00:37:17.520
teacher; provide instruction.

00:37:18.520 --> 00:37:22.320
And if he refuses

00:37:18.520 --> 00:37:22.320
to be a student?

00:37:22.400 --> 00:37:28.040
Then persist, gently,

00:37:22.400 --> 00:37:28.040
with humor, as is your manner.

00:37:30.280 --> 00:37:32.240
Make no mistake,

00:37:33.400 --> 00:37:37.920
should Guthrum

00:37:33.400 --> 00:37:37.920
ever consent to being baptized,

00:37:38.000 --> 00:37:42.480
then this war is over;

00:37:38.000 --> 00:37:42.480
England is ours.

00:37:45.400 --> 00:37:49.680
This would be

00:37:45.400 --> 00:37:49.680
truly God's work you do.

00:37:49.760 --> 00:37:55.200
Forgive me, Lord, but I cannot

00:37:49.760 --> 00:37:55.200
help but feel afraid.

00:37:56.280 --> 00:38:00.200
They are not content

00:37:56.280 --> 00:38:00.200
to simply kill a priest.

00:38:01.000 --> 00:38:04.160
Fear is within all of us...

00:38:05.720 --> 00:38:07.880
...as is strength.

00:38:10.120 --> 00:38:12.320
[retching]

00:38:37.560 --> 00:38:39.840
Lord, I would be

00:38:37.560 --> 00:38:39.840
more useful as a warrior,

00:38:39.920 --> 00:38:41.200
for when the truce fails.

00:38:41.280 --> 00:38:43.600
Oh, the truce will hold,

00:38:41.280 --> 00:38:43.600
for a time,

00:38:43.680 --> 00:38:45.520
and in that time you will be

00:38:45.600 --> 00:38:47.400
my eyes and ears

00:38:45.600 --> 00:38:47.400
inside the fortress.

00:38:47.480 --> 00:38:49.720
-Listening for what?

00:38:47.480 --> 00:38:49.720
-For Ubba.

00:38:49.800 --> 00:38:53.440
If and when you hear

00:38:49.800 --> 00:38:53.440
of his return, you'll escape.

00:38:53.520 --> 00:38:55.120
And if I'm in chains?

00:38:55.200 --> 00:38:57.200
Our men here shall disband,

00:38:55.200 --> 00:38:57.200
there are fields to work,

00:38:57.280 --> 00:38:59.120
but I will build

00:38:57.280 --> 00:38:59.120
a beacon on the hill;

00:38:59.200 --> 00:39:01.320
you will escape

00:38:59.200 --> 00:39:01.320
and light the fire.

00:39:01.400 --> 00:39:04.080
Lord, do you know that escape

00:39:01.400 --> 00:39:04.080
will be near impossible?

00:39:04.160 --> 00:39:08.720
If Ubba returns, the hostages will

00:39:04.160 --> 00:39:08.720
be killed and the Danes will attack.

00:39:08.800 --> 00:39:11.000
Upon sight of this

00:39:08.800 --> 00:39:11.000
first beacon being lit,

00:39:11.080 --> 00:39:13.600
other fires will start and the whole

00:39:11.080 --> 00:39:13.600
of Wessex will be called to arms.

00:39:13.680 --> 00:39:15.400
And if I refuse,

00:39:13.680 --> 00:39:15.400
to become a hostage?

00:39:15.480 --> 00:39:17.360
Then another man

00:39:15.480 --> 00:39:17.360
shall light the beacon.

00:39:17.840 --> 00:39:19.920
Why can't you accept me?

00:39:20.000 --> 00:39:21.960
I have been

00:39:20.000 --> 00:39:21.960
nothing but truthful to you;

00:39:22.040 --> 00:39:23.120
why am I always being

00:39:22.040 --> 00:39:23.120
put to the test?

00:39:23.200 --> 00:39:25.240
Why do you not show your king

00:39:23.200 --> 00:39:25.240
the respect that is due?

00:39:25.320 --> 00:39:29.120
Because you, Uhtred of Wherever,

00:39:25.320 --> 00:39:29.120
you do not see me as your king!

00:39:29.200 --> 00:39:31.680
You do not see

00:39:29.200 --> 00:39:31.680
my God as your God!

00:39:31.760 --> 00:39:32.760
Lord?

00:39:32.840 --> 00:39:34.520
I have not finished

00:39:32.840 --> 00:39:34.520
with you yet!

00:39:37.000 --> 00:39:39.880
Guthrum is waiting to hear

00:39:37.000 --> 00:39:39.880
of Ubba's return from Ireland.

00:39:39.960 --> 00:39:43.040
I need to know when this occurs,

00:39:39.960 --> 00:39:43.040
sooner rather than later.

00:39:43.120 --> 00:39:46.720
You... are the only man

00:39:46.800 --> 00:39:50.200
who could possibly provide

00:39:46.800 --> 00:39:50.200
this information sooner.

00:39:50.280 --> 00:39:56.240
Yes, it is possible that you will die,

00:39:50.280 --> 00:39:56.240
but it is likely that we shall all... die.

00:39:58.240 --> 00:40:00.280
You will go to the Danes.

00:40:00.360 --> 00:40:06.000
How you go, as a Saxon hostage or a

00:40:00.360 --> 00:40:06.000
Viking warrior, becomes your choice.

00:40:11.600 --> 00:40:13.440
I'll do as you ask.

00:40:16.600 --> 00:40:18.920
But if my child is born

00:40:16.600 --> 00:40:18.920
while I am captive,

00:40:19.000 --> 00:40:20.760
I ask that you send word.

00:40:20.840 --> 00:40:24.080
Of course,

00:40:20.840 --> 00:40:24.080
and should you die as a captive,

00:40:24.160 --> 00:40:27.000
rest assured the debt

00:40:24.160 --> 00:40:27.000
shall die with you.

00:40:41.040 --> 00:40:45.000
Will they treat us well?

00:40:41.040 --> 00:40:45.000
You are one of them.

00:40:46.040 --> 00:40:49.160
If I am one of them,

00:40:46.040 --> 00:40:49.160
then why am I a hostage?

00:40:49.760 --> 00:40:50.720
They'll treat us well,

00:40:50.800 --> 00:40:52.440
for as long as the truce holds.

00:40:52.520 --> 00:40:54.000
If it fails?

00:40:54.080 --> 00:40:57.000
They will kill us all,

00:40:54.080 --> 00:40:57.000
starting with the priest.

00:40:57.080 --> 00:40:58.720
[chuckle]

00:40:58.800 --> 00:41:01.880
I have made my peace.

00:40:58.800 --> 00:41:01.880
I am ready.

00:41:01.960 --> 00:41:04.640
Good evening,

00:41:01.960 --> 00:41:04.640
and God bless you all.

00:41:05.800 --> 00:41:07.680
Poor wretches.

00:41:07.760 --> 00:41:09.480
And, us, Father, what are we?

00:41:09.560 --> 00:41:12.080
We are fortunate, Lord.

00:41:09.560 --> 00:41:12.080
We know God.

00:41:12.160 --> 00:41:15.360
Although granted,

00:41:12.160 --> 00:41:15.360
I'm in no hurry to meet him.

00:41:15.440 --> 00:41:18.040
Let us pray he feels the same.

00:41:18.120 --> 00:41:19.440
Amen.

00:41:37.720 --> 00:41:40.680
[indistinct yelling]

00:41:44.880 --> 00:41:48.720
Is this rabble

00:41:44.880 --> 00:41:48.720
what so many are afraid of?

00:41:48.800 --> 00:41:51.320
They are like children!

00:41:56.000 --> 00:41:59.160
Enough. Enough!

00:42:00.080 --> 00:42:03.040
They're our guests,

00:42:00.080 --> 00:42:03.040
for a while.

00:42:03.640 --> 00:42:06.080
There's one rule only:

00:42:06.160 --> 00:42:10.840
At nightfall, you will gather

00:42:06.160 --> 00:42:10.840
and sleep at the church;

00:42:10.920 --> 00:42:13.400
the doors will be barred.

00:42:14.320 --> 00:42:16.080
At daybreak,

00:42:14.320 --> 00:42:16.080
you will then free

00:42:16.160 --> 00:42:19.960
to walk, talk, jump,

00:42:16.160 --> 00:42:19.960
hump, carry weapons.

00:42:20.040 --> 00:42:23.680
My men have orders

00:42:20.040 --> 00:42:23.680
not to kill you...

00:42:24.680 --> 00:42:27.720
...unless you deserve

00:42:24.680 --> 00:42:27.720
to be killed.

00:42:31.880 --> 00:42:36.520
I am Guthrum.. and one day

00:42:31.880 --> 00:42:36.520
I shall be your king.

00:42:36.600 --> 00:42:38.640
Do you understand

00:42:36.600 --> 00:42:38.640
what I have said?

00:42:38.720 --> 00:42:41.280
You will all say, "Yes, Lord."

00:42:42.040 --> 00:42:44.280
[all]

00:42:42.040 --> 00:42:44.280
Yes, Lord.

00:42:44.360 --> 00:42:46.560
I did not hear you.

00:42:51.560 --> 00:42:53.600
I understand you, Lord.

00:42:53.680 --> 00:42:56.840
Maybe I will make

00:42:53.680 --> 00:42:56.840
a present of you to Ubba.

00:42:56.920 --> 00:42:58.840
Should he ever return

00:42:56.920 --> 00:42:58.840
from Ireland.

00:42:58.920 --> 00:43:00.880
He may not, that's possible.

00:43:00.960 --> 00:43:03.440
But then his men

00:43:00.960 --> 00:43:03.440
will become my men,

00:43:03.520 --> 00:43:07.040
and I will honor him

00:43:03.520 --> 00:43:07.040
by killing you myself.

00:43:08.520 --> 00:43:10.520
With arrows, perhaps.

00:43:10.600 --> 00:43:13.400
-Ragnar Ragnarson!

00:43:10.600 --> 00:43:13.400
-Here.

00:43:13.480 --> 00:43:16.480
You know this one well;

00:43:13.480 --> 00:43:16.480
keep him out of my sight.

00:43:16.560 --> 00:43:19.600
Take them to the church;

00:43:16.560 --> 00:43:19.600
feed them.

00:43:26.680 --> 00:43:29.200
Now you are where you belong.

00:43:29.280 --> 00:43:30.960
Now I'm with my brother.

00:43:31.040 --> 00:43:32.360
I will remind you

00:43:31.040 --> 00:43:32.360
what it is like

00:43:32.440 --> 00:43:35.200
to be a Dane

00:43:32.440 --> 00:43:35.200
and make you stay.

00:43:35.920 --> 00:43:38.000
Brida is here.

00:43:56.400 --> 00:43:59.360
I dream about you, vixen.

00:44:00.840 --> 00:44:03.160
I'm not surprised to hear it.

00:44:04.080 --> 00:44:06.400
You've grown up.

00:44:04.080 --> 00:44:06.400
[chuckles]

00:44:09.960 --> 00:44:11.920
You should know

00:44:09.960 --> 00:44:11.920
I'm with Ragnar now.

00:44:12.000 --> 00:44:13.720
He's my man.

00:44:14.400 --> 00:44:19.160
That's good.

00:44:14.400 --> 00:44:19.160
That's good.

00:44:21.120 --> 00:44:23.760
You should know

00:44:21.120 --> 00:44:23.760
that I'm married.

00:44:24.680 --> 00:44:28.720
Married! You have grown up!

00:44:28.800 --> 00:44:32.200
-He is married?

00:44:28.800 --> 00:44:32.200
-Yes, he is married!

00:44:32.280 --> 00:44:35.200
Time is moving quicker

00:44:32.280 --> 00:44:35.200
than I thought;

00:44:35.280 --> 00:44:38.920
tonight we get drunk, we must!

00:44:39.000 --> 00:44:41.560
I need to be inside the church.

00:44:41.640 --> 00:44:43.760
No, tonight we get drunk,

00:44:43.840 --> 00:44:48.840
I'll take you to the church myself,

00:44:43.840 --> 00:44:48.840
or we sleep where we fall.

00:44:48.920 --> 00:44:53.480
And...

00:44:48.920 --> 00:44:53.480
we must talk of the future.

00:44:53.560 --> 00:44:56.080
[cheering]

00:45:01.320 --> 00:45:03.400
[men grunting]

00:45:08.240 --> 00:45:10.880
We are oarsmen!

00:45:10.960 --> 00:45:13.840
Pull! Pull!

00:45:13.920 --> 00:45:16.200
Uhtred, pull for me.

00:45:16.640 --> 00:45:17.880
I need to piss.

00:45:17.960 --> 00:45:20.320
I'll return later.

00:45:20.960 --> 00:45:23.720
Ragnar, Ragnar!

00:45:30.080 --> 00:45:32.560
[all laughing]

00:45:36.600 --> 00:45:39.800
I haven't laughed

00:45:36.600 --> 00:45:39.800
so much in a long time.

00:45:39.880 --> 00:45:41.720
Then you haven't been living.

00:45:41.800 --> 00:45:45.160
Or as Ravn would say,

00:45:41.800 --> 00:45:45.160
"Tomorrow we die."

00:45:45.240 --> 00:45:47.320
When did he ever say that?

00:45:47.400 --> 00:45:50.040
When you were out chopping wood.

00:45:51.000 --> 00:45:53.480
Oh...

00:45:53.560 --> 00:45:58.200
Well, I actually

00:45:53.560 --> 00:45:58.200
do need to piss.

00:45:58.280 --> 00:46:01.680
What you need to do

00:45:58.280 --> 00:46:01.680
is to stop drinking.

00:46:01.760 --> 00:46:04.120
Tomorrow we die!

00:46:10.840 --> 00:46:13.240
-He's happy to see you.

00:46:10.840 --> 00:46:13.240
-I've missed him.

00:46:16.960 --> 00:46:18.440
I miss you both.

00:46:26.800 --> 00:46:28.880
Are you his wife?

00:46:29.320 --> 00:46:30.720
I'm with him.

00:46:32.400 --> 00:46:34.920
-Is she beautiful?

00:46:32.400 --> 00:46:34.920
-Hmm...

00:46:35.000 --> 00:46:38.520
Her name is Mildrith.

00:46:35.000 --> 00:46:38.520
Yes, she is beautiful.

00:46:42.120 --> 00:46:44.600
She carries my child.

00:46:49.720 --> 00:46:51.960
Who decided you should marry?

00:46:53.360 --> 00:46:55.200
Alfred.

00:46:57.880 --> 00:47:00.520
I have the land I asked for,

00:46:57.880 --> 00:47:00.520
in Wessex.

00:47:04.440 --> 00:47:08.160
You swear an oath to Alfred.

00:47:04.440 --> 00:47:08.160
You marry for Alfred.

00:47:08.240 --> 00:47:10.560
You have land

00:47:08.240 --> 00:47:10.560
given to you by Alfred.

00:47:10.640 --> 00:47:12.560
Your wife carries your child,

00:47:12.640 --> 00:47:16.000
and yet you are given up

00:47:12.640 --> 00:47:16.000
as a hostage by Alfred?

00:47:16.680 --> 00:47:19.080
Are you a spy, Uhtred?

00:47:22.440 --> 00:47:25.160
The first sign of Ubba

00:47:22.440 --> 00:47:25.160
returning, I am to escape.

00:47:26.880 --> 00:47:29.200
But I know

00:47:26.880 --> 00:47:29.200
that when Ubba returns

00:47:29.280 --> 00:47:32.160
the hostages will be killed.

00:47:32.240 --> 00:47:34.720
[scoffs]

00:47:32.240 --> 00:47:34.720
Alfred's not fond of me.

00:47:34.800 --> 00:47:37.440
Refuse him.

00:47:37.520 --> 00:47:39.760
refuse to be a hostage, join us.

00:47:41.720 --> 00:47:45.760
I should ask you, Uhtred,

00:47:41.720 --> 00:47:45.760
not that it matters,

00:47:45.840 --> 00:47:47.880
but I should ask.

00:47:47.960 --> 00:47:50.760
Is it a problem to you

00:47:47.960 --> 00:47:50.760
that Brida is with me now?

00:47:53.440 --> 00:47:54.360
[laughs]

00:47:54.440 --> 00:47:56.520
No, I'm happy about it.

00:47:56.960 --> 00:47:58.680
I swear.

00:47:58.760 --> 00:47:59.760
Alright.

00:47:59.840 --> 00:48:02.080
Not that she cares

00:47:59.840 --> 00:48:02.080
what you think.

00:48:02.160 --> 00:48:03.800
I would hump her regardless.

00:48:03.880 --> 00:48:06.680
[grunts]

00:48:03.880 --> 00:48:06.680
With affection.

00:48:06.760 --> 00:48:10.080
-And with my permission.

00:48:06.760 --> 00:48:10.080
-I know.

00:48:11.840 --> 00:48:13.960
Do you know Uhtred's

00:48:11.840 --> 00:48:13.960
to be a father?

00:48:16.480 --> 00:48:19.760
A father... When?

00:48:19.840 --> 00:48:22.120
Soon, I am told.

00:48:23.040 --> 00:48:25.920
You would want to see it.

00:48:26.000 --> 00:48:30.360
Yes, I hope to return

00:48:26.000 --> 00:48:30.360
to my wife and child.

00:48:32.640 --> 00:48:37.960
Ragnar, I'll be with you

00:48:32.640 --> 00:48:37.960
to avenge our father.

00:48:38.040 --> 00:48:39.400
Kjartan will pay.

00:48:39.480 --> 00:48:42.520
You should have joined me

00:48:39.480 --> 00:48:42.520
months ago, with Brida.

00:48:42.600 --> 00:48:44.200
I'd sworn an oath.

00:48:44.280 --> 00:48:46.960
To a poxy Saxon king!

00:48:47.040 --> 00:48:49.360
Ubba wanted to see me dead,

00:48:47.040 --> 00:48:49.360
there was nowhere else to go.

00:48:49.440 --> 00:48:51.400
You know, I have thought about

00:48:49.440 --> 00:48:51.400
that night in the woods.

00:48:51.480 --> 00:48:54.280
You had the choice to be

00:48:51.480 --> 00:48:54.280
a Saxon or a Dane.

00:48:54.360 --> 00:48:56.200
No, no I had sworn an oath.

00:48:57.160 --> 00:48:59.600
You should have joined me.

00:48:59.680 --> 00:49:03.160
I'll be with you

00:48:59.680 --> 00:49:03.160
to kill Kjartan.

00:49:05.840 --> 00:49:09.440
I will take you to the church.

00:49:09.520 --> 00:49:11.200
To your bed.

00:49:13.560 --> 00:49:17.400
[Mildrith screaming, panting]

00:49:26.520 --> 00:49:28.720
[grunts]

00:49:35.920 --> 00:49:38.240
[baby crying]

00:49:38.320 --> 00:49:40.960
-What is it?

00:49:38.320 --> 00:49:40.960
-It's a son, lady.

00:49:41.040 --> 00:49:43.240
A handsome boy.

00:49:48.000 --> 00:49:51.600
You will be Uhtred,

00:49:48.000 --> 00:49:51.600
son of Uhtred.

00:50:00.240 --> 00:50:02.360
Good morning, Uhtred.

00:50:03.080 --> 00:50:05.160
Morning, Father.

00:50:05.920 --> 00:50:07.840
Raining again.

00:50:07.920 --> 00:50:09.720
One day seems like the next.

00:50:09.800 --> 00:50:11.520
[yawns]

00:50:11.600 --> 00:50:13.200
It does.

00:50:14.400 --> 00:50:17.640
Still, at least,

00:50:14.400 --> 00:50:17.640
we're alive to feel it.

00:50:18.680 --> 00:50:21.160
How are your

00:50:18.680 --> 00:50:21.160
conversations with Guthrum?

00:50:21.240 --> 00:50:23.360
Is he a Christian yet?

00:50:23.440 --> 00:50:26.840
I believe that time is near, I do.

00:50:26.920 --> 00:50:30.680
I often leave him to contemplate alone,

00:50:26.920 --> 00:50:30.680
in church.

00:50:30.760 --> 00:50:35.400
Guthrum likes to contemplate

00:50:30.760 --> 00:50:35.400
war and kingdoms.

00:50:35.480 --> 00:50:40.400
The kingdom of Heaven is his

00:50:35.480 --> 00:50:40.400
to share, I have told him.

00:50:42.040 --> 00:50:44.240
A man can change, Uhtred.

00:50:47.760 --> 00:50:48.960
Onward.

00:50:49.040 --> 00:50:51.960
God Bless you.

00:50:49.040 --> 00:50:51.960
May you enjoy a good day.

00:50:52.040 --> 00:50:53.840
Thank you, Father.

00:50:54.600 --> 00:50:58.160
He is the king of kings,

00:50:58.240 --> 00:51:01.400
capable of great,

00:50:58.240 --> 00:51:01.400
great things.

00:51:01.480 --> 00:51:05.440
-Such as what?

00:51:01.480 --> 00:51:05.440
-Such as miracles.

00:51:05.520 --> 00:51:08.200
[chuckles]

00:51:05.520 --> 00:51:08.200
Miracles!

00:51:08.600 --> 00:51:10.480
Such as what?

00:51:10.560 --> 00:51:14.720
Such as... you, Lord.

00:51:15.680 --> 00:51:18.920
You are a miracle.

00:51:19.000 --> 00:51:23.680
He has made you strong,

00:51:19.000 --> 00:51:23.680
yet merciful.

00:51:23.760 --> 00:51:30.320
He has... made you proud,

00:51:23.760 --> 00:51:30.320
yet humble.

00:51:30.400 --> 00:51:33.120
He has made you eager to learn.

00:51:34.400 --> 00:51:36.560
He has given you free will,

00:51:36.640 --> 00:51:38.560
hoping that you will

00:51:36.640 --> 00:51:38.560
find the courage

00:51:38.640 --> 00:51:41.440
to choose him above all else.

00:51:41.520 --> 00:51:43.640
And, I believe,

00:51:43.720 --> 00:51:47.040
I truly believe,

00:51:43.720 --> 00:51:47.040
he will been rewarded.

00:51:47.120 --> 00:51:49.200
[gate opens]

00:51:54.160 --> 00:51:57.560
-I have a message for Guthrum.

00:51:54.160 --> 00:51:57.560
-He's in the church.

00:52:12.720 --> 00:52:14.320
Lord, may I speak?

00:52:15.080 --> 00:52:16.360
Freely.

00:52:16.440 --> 00:52:18.040
Ubba and his army

00:52:16.440 --> 00:52:18.040
have returned from Ireland.

00:52:18.120 --> 00:52:22.000
They are coming ashore

00:52:18.120 --> 00:52:22.000
north of here, at the Severn.

00:52:22.080 --> 00:52:24.080
And my fleet is where?

00:52:24.160 --> 00:52:27.080
They left Lundene several days

00:52:24.160 --> 00:52:27.080
ago and are nearly here, Lord.

00:52:27.160 --> 00:52:30.640
Every last ship will be here,

00:52:27.160 --> 00:52:30.640
every man will be with you.

00:52:30.720 --> 00:52:32.920
That is good news.

00:52:37.000 --> 00:52:37.880
[groans]

00:52:37.960 --> 00:52:40.040
I dispatch you to your heaven.

00:52:42.920 --> 00:52:45.160
No need to thank me.

00:53:01.080 --> 00:53:02.720
Father...

00:53:03.920 --> 00:53:07.800
Ubba has returned.

00:53:03.920 --> 00:53:07.800
Did they say?

00:53:09.880 --> 00:53:11.840
[weakly] Yes.

00:53:13.520 --> 00:53:16.320
[Guthrum]

00:53:13.520 --> 00:53:16.320
Men, the peace is over.

00:53:16.400 --> 00:53:18.000
Prepare for battle.

00:53:18.080 --> 00:53:20.520
[men cheering]

00:53:26.840 --> 00:53:30.840
The Saxon hostages,

00:53:26.840 --> 00:53:30.840
kill them all.

00:53:30.920 --> 00:53:32.920
[grunting and groaning]

00:53:33.000 --> 00:53:34.960
Catch him!

00:53:35.720 --> 00:53:38.240
Cut him to pieces!

00:53:42.720 --> 00:53:44.320
[yelling]

00:53:56.800 --> 00:53:58.240
[screams]

00:53:59.800 --> 00:54:03.880
Leave him! I say leave him!

00:54:05.080 --> 00:54:11.320
Ragnar, please, step aside.

00:54:11.400 --> 00:54:14.320
You know all the hostages

00:54:11.400 --> 00:54:14.320
have to die.

00:54:14.400 --> 00:54:15.720
[Young Ragnar]

00:54:14.400 --> 00:54:15.720
Then kill him!

00:54:15.800 --> 00:54:17.600
You're welcome to kill him,

00:54:17.680 --> 00:54:18.920
but you have to kill me first.

00:54:19.000 --> 00:54:22.960
I could've happily

00:54:19.000 --> 00:54:22.960
managed without this.

00:54:23.040 --> 00:54:26.800
He's a Saxon.

00:54:23.040 --> 00:54:26.800
He's a traitor. He's an enemy.

00:54:26.880 --> 00:54:29.640
Well, to get to him,

00:54:26.880 --> 00:54:29.640
you have to kill me.

00:54:31.400 --> 00:54:34.960
My men,

00:54:31.400 --> 00:54:34.960
they will not follow you.

00:54:46.240 --> 00:54:49.120
I will give you one last charity.

00:54:50.040 --> 00:54:53.080
Release him, without a horse.

00:55:03.280 --> 00:55:05.160
Are you alright?

00:55:05.920 --> 00:55:07.680
I have no words.

00:55:07.760 --> 00:55:10.080
You should go.

00:55:07.760 --> 00:55:10.080
Go and see your child.

00:55:10.160 --> 00:55:11.920
Go.

00:55:13.920 --> 00:55:15.640
Yes.

00:55:16.160 --> 00:55:18.000
I'll be with you.

00:55:19.240 --> 00:55:21.120
Both of you.